{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>הערה.</b> גִּלָּה — and likewise every instance of the term עֶרְוָה is גִּלּוּי, uncovering. The vav descends in the word for a structural reason, as in זַעֲוָה, derived from a root without the vav — ״וְלֹא קָם וְלֹא זָע״ (Esther 5) — and likewise אַחֲוָה, derived from אָח. As for הַעֲרָאָה — our Sages disagreed about it: some say it is נְשִׁיקַת שַׁמָּשׁ, and some say it is הַכְנָסַת עֲטָרָה (Yevamot 55)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:27.651089532Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}